cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Correlation-Weighted Cyclical Z-Score Imputation (CW-CZI)
message: If you use this software or its benchmark, please cite the article below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kotan
    given-names: Kurban
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6660-0565
    affiliation: Manisa Celal Bayar University
    email: kurban.kotan@cbu.edu.tr
abstract: >-
  CW-CZI is a model-free imputer for numerical tabular data. It fills each
  missing cell from a correlation-weighted combination of the standardised
  values observed in the same row and refreshes the column moments and the
  correlation matrix once per cycle. The repository holds the estimator, the
  benchmark behind the accompanying article (eleven datasets; MCAR, MAR and
  MNAR), its raw output, and the scripts that turn that output into every
  table and figure of the article.
repository-code: https://github.com/kurbankotan/CW-CZI
license: MIT
version: "7.0"
date-released: 2026-11-02
keywords:
  - missing data
  - imputation
  - tabular data
  - correlation weighting
  - z-score
  - model-free estimation
  - MCAR
  - MAR
  - MNAR
  - benchmark
